WEBVTT

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.570
Really? That's--

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.990
Well, y'know.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.400
'Morning, Yuno and Miyako.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.920
Good morning!

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.870
Wow, Sae, you're up early.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:12.980
I was up until dawn, but I'm still in the habit of waking up now.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.880
I'm glad I got up in time to see you two off.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.150
It feels so weird that we're going and you're staying here...

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.350
Hiro must still be asleep.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.800
Well, tomorrow's the last time she'll have to get up early to make it to school.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.030
You'd better hurry, before the bell rings.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:34.990
All right, let's get going!

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:36.490
See you.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:37.740
Here we go!

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:59.160
Peachy warm glow of the spring sky

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.720
Toasty summer sun blazing down on our skin

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.470
Fickle autumn sky just like a maiden's heart

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.100
Shivery winter

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.570
So, what's this year's hot color?

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:12.230
The perfect shade to go with girls' talk

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:15.030
Marble, colorful, a miracle

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:17.490
Wait, what were we talking about?

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.640
I hate the rain~

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:20.250
I've got an umbrella!

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.300
Today's sunny!

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.730
Let's race all the way home!

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.970
Let's go all the way up to four stars this time

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:25.450
(Hee-hee)

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:32.090
Time to give all the teachers a shock like they've never had! (Oh!)

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.500
Since we're all friends, everything's friendly

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.960
Every day's just so wonderful

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.590
Delicious, exciting, fascinating

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:42.510
Art is our gift

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:45.010
Want to smile together more than ever before

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:48.720
Coming together into a circle like the sun

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.860
A marvelous combination

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:58.280
Come on, let's hold hands

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.570
Like it? Love it love it sketch it!

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:06.060
Paint it all the colors of the rainbow!

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.570
All right, let's go!

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.500
What's wrong, Yuno?

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.200
You've looked depressed all day.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.750
Aren't you feeling lonely?

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:42.610
I can't believe Sae and Hiro are graduating and then moving out next month.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.560
Well, moping around isn't gonna change things.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.580
You know what we can do?

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.790
We can be happy for them, and celebrate!

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.290
Miya...

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:03.990
Hey, everyone.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:04.890
'Sup?

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.800
Oh, hi, Landlady!

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.890
I brought some pizza over to help celebrate.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:13.770
Tonight's a pre-graduation party with the landlady!

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:20.220
Sae, Hiro, congratulations on graduating!

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.200
Thanks.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.970
Cheers!

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:29.040
Thanks for everything you've done for us these three years.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:34.540
I never thought I'd be able to share a beer with you two.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.620
Just because we've graduated doesn't mean we're adults yet...

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.220
Aww, c'mon.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.670
When you two showed up here, you were this tiny!

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.430
I don't think we were quite that small...

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.810
You were like two little kids out of the sticks,

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.940
and now look how you've cleaned up.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:57.860
These here are proof of just how much Hiro's grown over the past three years!

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.150
Miya!

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:09.300
So, Sae, Hiro, what was it like when you two first met?

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.330
Were you always this close?

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.500
I, uh, don't even remember. How about you, Hiro?

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:20.250
Really, Sae, you don't?

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:24.380
I seem to remember something about "sugar and spice"...

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.280
<i>She's never in when I come by.</i>

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:35.480
<i>I just want to say "hi" after moving in...</i>

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.410
<i>Tomorrow's the entrance ceremony. </i>

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:55.180
<i>And I still haven't met the girl downstairs.</i>

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.300
<i>I wonder what she's like?</i>

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.200
<i>I can't believe she won't even come to the door...</i>

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:04.170
<i>What if she's a real weirdo?</i>

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:08.680
<i>What do I do? How can I spend three years with someone like that?</i>

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:34.370
All right, now line up single file and head on in!

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:49.260
<i>Wait, that isn't Riri or Misato!</i>

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.260
<i>Maybe it's--</i>

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.790
Um...

00:06:57.420 --> 00:06:58.270
Yes?

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:02.770
Are you one of the freshmen who just moved into Hidamari Apartments?

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:03.770
Yeah.

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:08.650
Great, I finally caught up with you...

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:16.160
Sorry to bother you.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.810
Sorry it's such a mess.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:22.840
No, I should be apologizing to you.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:25.680
I was just so excited to finally meet you that I...

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:29.330
Have a seat.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.350
What're you working on?

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.600
Oh, this? I've got a competition entry due by tomorrow.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:42.730
You write stories?

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:43.510
Yeah.

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:50.610
I've been cooped up in here because of the deadline, so I haven't had the chance to meet anyone yet.

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.360
Sorry.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:53.660
Don't worry.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:55.390
I'm just happy...

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:59.650
I mean, I'd heard at school that Hidamari Apartment tends to attract weirdos...

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:04.380
So I was worried you might be one of them.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:08.630
I was just tied up with this.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:13.980
So, will you have your manuscript done on time?

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:17.440
Yeah, I managed to finish it. All I have to do now is send it in.

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:21.390
Honestly, I've been up all night and sleeping during the day, so I'm exhausted right now.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.770
And that's why you couldn't come to the door...

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:28.270
You did make it to school today, though, right?

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:30.030
You saw me?

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:36.070
Do you mind if I take a peek at your story?

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:39.790
I guess...

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.380
Wake up!

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:58.640
Sorry, I drifted off.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:01.890
So you read it?

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.390
Yep! I couldn't put it down!

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:09.140
You're amazing! I could never write something like this!

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.290
You're like a pro!

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.460
Thanks...

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:14.650
Oh?

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:20.930
Have you been eating properly lately?

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:22.500
You're so skinny...

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:26.560
Well, sometimes I get so busy that I forget to eat...

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:27.550
I see...

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.570
That's no good!

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.490
Why don't I make something for you?

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:36.030
No! I mean, I can't impose like that.

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.630
Don't worry about it!

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.850
I have to cook dinner anyway.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:47.940
Well... I don't know how it'll come out, since I'm still getting used to cooking for myself, but...

00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:50.190
Thanks.

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:56.320
Cooking for someone else will help me learn better, too.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:59.410
I'm glad we get along so well.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:04.720
I hope we have a great time in high school together, uh...

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:06.210
Sae-chan?

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:07.960
Just call me Sae.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:14.090
I'm happy to meet you, too, Hiro-chan.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.590
You can just call me Hiro.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:27.100
I can definitely see them meeting like that.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:32.370
Wow, Hiro, I thought you were always good at cooking.

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:35.420
Did you really start learning after you moved in?

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:36.600
Yes.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:40.610
Having Sae along to taste-test helped me learn bit by bit.

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:43.120
So you'll be fine too, Nazuna!

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:43.990
Thanks!

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.620
I'll taste-test for you today!

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:55.380
And if this isn't the perfect time to introduce you to the "Sunflowers of Hidamari Apartments" association!

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:58.010
Sunflowers...

00:10:58.010 --> 00:10:59.380
Of Hidamari Apartments?

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.390
That's a thing?

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:06.670
Of course! You all practically grew up together here!

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:10.980
It'd be a shame if you graduated, went off, and never saw each other again.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:15.190
Let's all join together to support the kids at Hidamari Apartments!

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:17.590
Sure!

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:35.870
Hiro.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:40.590
Let's go.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:49.300
Is everyone ready?

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:49.990
Yeah!

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:51.060
Ready to go!

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:56.180
What's up with your skirt, Yunocchi?

00:11:56.920 --> 00:12:00.430
I thought I'd be prepared...

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:13.790
Yamabuki Private High School will now present its diplomas.

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:30.730
On a fresh spring day, I met you

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:35.800
The flowers in my heart were in full bloom

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:39.560
Congratulations to today's graduates of Yamabuki Private High School.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:42.790
I can see the cherry blossoms from the window

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:44.990
What are your memories of three years here at Yamabuki?

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:50.130
Memories of growth, both of the body and the mind?

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:52.030
As our second spring passes, my feelings haven't changed

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:55.300
Memories of bonds forged with your classmates through shared experiences?

00:12:52.030 --> 00:12:57.200
Let's walk the distance that remains between us

00:12:55.300 --> 00:13:01.010
No matter how these years have changed you, they lay a foundation for the rest of your life.

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:02.780
Pretending it was just by chance,

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:08.100
As you leave your cradle here at Yamabuki, and as you mature into adults over the next two years,

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:06.730
I waited on your path home

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:13.110
The petals dancing on my palm,

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:15.390
responsibility for the future of Japan will pass into your hands.

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:16.220
your smile;

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:19.570
Life is not smooth sailing.

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:20.320
this scene is still burned into my eyes

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:24.590
A long road lies before you, full of setbacks and challenges.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.710
Blossom, cherry blossoms

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:26.220
I want to be with you

00:13:24.590 --> 00:13:29.910
However, those challenges are also chances to succeed.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:34.380
As long as I'm around you, the cherry blossoms bloom

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:37.420
As your path through life stretches out before you, may you always find happiness.

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:45.630
I love this bright, shining season

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:05.940
Sae! Hiro! We graduated!

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:09.700
Let's get together once in a while! We should keep in touch!

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:13.200
Yeah! Let's stay friends forever!

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:16.460
Nakatani, can we talk?

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:21.710
You don't need to back off like that!

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:26.600
Hold on, I need to use the restroom.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:29.090
Wait, Sae, are you going to go confess to someone!?

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.760
What're you talking about?

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.350
My eyes are a little puffy...

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:41.110
Natsume?

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:42.980
Sae!

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:46.940
It... It's not like I came here to meet you or anything!

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:50.410
Obviously. I mean, this is the bathroom.

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.530
Congratulations.

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:56.880
Thanks.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:57.910
You too.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.760
We'll be going to different colleges.

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:06.000
So I guess this is the last time we meet at school.

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:11.180
But our colleges are close... So...

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:23.130
I... I mean, now, my college is close to home... So...

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:30.470
Yeah. We'll stay in touch.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:42.830
Huh?

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:45.540
Sae, your eyes are all red now.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.460
No way.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:52.920
We're all signing each other's yearbooks.

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:53.970
You should write something too, Sae!

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:55.220
Sure!

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.140
Here's mine, too!

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:10.820
Let's go home.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.350
Sae! Hiro!

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:14.860
Miss Yoshinoya!

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:17.780
Congratulations!

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:20.760
You did so much for us.

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:24.370
Thanks for everything.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:28.210
I hope I can become as good of a teacher as you are someday.

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:30.340
Sae... Hiro...

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:36.010
Please, never forget the feel of my body!

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:38.600
That just sounds wrong.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.940
Sec, I think I've got a text.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:46.100
Me too.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:47.740
It's from Mom.

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:49.360
Me too.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:54.110
Why are they exactly the same?

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:00.000
They could have at least come up and said hi.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:05.000
They're probably talking about things we did when we were little...

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:06.260
Yeah.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:08.950
Hey, why don't we both reply with exactly the same thing?

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:10.130
Good idea.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:19.370
Thanks for sending us to Yamabuki High.

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:27.990
Really?

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:31.780
You waited for us?

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:34.210
We said you didn't have to wait around...

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:37.030
Sae... Hiro...

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:38.910
One, two...

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:45.290
Don't graduate! We don't want you to graduate!

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:49.300
Are you sure you have enough credits? Maybe you need to stay back a year!

00:17:49.300 --> 00:17:50.440
That's right!

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.980
Stop saying that! It's scary!

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:55.400
You don't have to stay until me and Nazuna graduate!

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:57.170
One more year is enough!

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:58.380
Can't we stay together?

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:00.050
No graduation!

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:04.430
Sae, Hiro, why not be seniors again?

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:10.080
Actually, why don't you stay for us and be seniors two more times!?

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:11.520
That's a great idea!

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:14.650
I really, really don't want you to graduate!

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:21.010
That's three minutes.

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:22.240
That was so fast...

00:18:25.290 --> 00:18:28.370
We decided we'd be selfish for three minutes.

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:31.790
All right! Time to change over!

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:33.380
Sae! Hiro!

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:34.380
Yes?

00:18:34.990 --> 00:18:38.130
Congratulations!

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:41.340
Thanks.

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:48.390
It feels strange walking home together like this now.

00:18:49.340 --> 00:18:51.790
What shall we do for dinner?

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:54.190
Let's make sushi!

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:00.350
I've had so much fun these three years.

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:02.280
Me too.

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:07.090
We've always been so cheerful together, at school and at home.

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:11.270
Even when I've felt depressed, you've been there to hold me up.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:17.440
I left my family when I moved to Hidamari Apartments,

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:23.820
but I was able to get through all the times I felt lonely thanks to Sae and Hiro and Miya.

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:27.120
And then came Nori and Nazuna.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:29.920
Spending every day together felt like the most natural thing in the world.

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:33.680
Eating together, going out together...

00:19:34.390 --> 00:19:38.820
I don't really know how to say it, but we became something more than friends.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:41.950
You're all so, so special to me...

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:44.730
So we're like family?

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:49.710
That's right. We're like a family now.

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:51.920
Yeah!

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:58.630
If Sae's the dad, and Hiro's the mom, then I must be...

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.130
Guess I'm the dog.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:01.020
Arf!

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.050
Sounds about right.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:08.640
It's so... warm and comfortable here.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:12.640
And if we're a family, we'll still be connected even if we're not physically together.

00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:17.650
You're right!

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:23.590
Had enough to eat?

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:27.960
That sushi was great.

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:31.040
I hope next time I do better at rolling it.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:33.700
You squash the rice too much!

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:34.500
Really?

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:35.630
Yeah.

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:41.380
Miya... Thanks for being by my side.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:48.060
I wish I could be someone like Sae or Hiro, always there with a smile, setting a good example...

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:51.480
I wish I could choose a dream and work for it like they did.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:56.650
I look up to them so much... I want to help them succeed so much...

00:20:57.140 --> 00:21:02.150
That's why I'm really happy they graduated.

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:06.490
It will be kind of lonely around here, though.

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:07.660
Yeah.

00:21:44.470 --> 00:21:49.010
<i>I've met so many people since I came to Hidamari Apartments...</i>

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:53.350
<i>So many people that I care for so, so much.</i>

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:03.330
<i>What will tomorrow bring?</i>

00:22:24.390 --> 00:22:30.060
That warmth that's always right there waiting next to me

00:22:30.060 --> 00:22:36.390
Just a ten-second walk away from where I am now

00:22:36.390 --> 00:22:41.990
Whenever I feel empty we can just get together

00:22:41.990 --> 00:22:49.520
And the loneliness I feel just flies out the window

00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:55.880
Day by day, season by season

00:22:55.880 --> 00:23:00.280
I realize something new

00:23:00.280 --> 00:23:02.640
"Good morning", "Good night"

00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:05.670
"Let's hang out again tomorrow"

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:12.050
People who know me better than I know myself

00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:17.710
The memories that blossom lit up by those smiles

00:23:17.710 --> 00:23:25.000
Beaming down on me, they're my sunshine
